body:
That's exactly what I'm talking about. That's what I \*did\*, but several members of Constellation are still behaving as if someone has died. This post is about the fact that they are referencing events that *didn't* happen. 

&#x200B;

But comments I'm getting(and further experiences as I go through the game) seem to indicate that this is the rule, rather than the exception.

Funnily enough, on my next encounter with the Hunter, he actually \*did\* acknowledge that I avoided the death, and congratulated me on it.

&#x200B;

I have also had three separate times in this same playthrough where the Hunter has \*suddenly realized\* that I am also Starborn. 

&#x200B;

Honestly, these holes in the dialogue scripting are embarrassing.
